    """Delete a directory tree.

    If the optional argument `ignore_errors` is true, errors are ignored;
    otherwise, if on Windows, rmtree() will try to remove read-only files.

    If you don't need to know whether the directory was deleted or not (i.e.
    you're just removing a temporary directory), `rmtree()` is the right
    function to use. It's recursive, too: it will delete subdirectories,
    too.

    """
